# Answer key for B3 t4_adversarial.sql - DML-specific traps.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# The forbidden list is the test. Conventions: B1/B2 plus D-15..D-18 (not implemented).

@ 20 S1 a target alias spelled like another table
value dim_store.country_code -> dim_store.region identity
filter customers.status -> dim_store
forbid value customers.country_code -> dim_store.region | `customers` in the SET is the TARGET alias (dim_store); staging.customers is `c`
forbid filter customers.country_code -> dim_store | `c.country_code = customers.country_code` joins the FROM list to the target (D-11)

@ 30 S2 EXCLUDED is the proposed row
value customers.id -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value customers.country_code -> customer_summary.segment identity
forbid value customers.segment -> customer_summary.segment | EXCLUDED.segment is the value PROPOSED for segment - x.country_code - not the source's own segment column

@ 40 S3 the target joined to itself
value dim_customer.first_order_date -> dim_customer.first_order_date identity
filter dim_customer.is_current -> dim_customer
forbid filter dim_customer.customer_id -> dim_customer | the self-join key joins FROM to the target (D-11)

@ 52 S4 two SETs reading each other's OLD values
value dim_product.cost -> dim_product.list_price derived
value dim_product.list_price -> dim_product.cost identity
forbid value dim_product.cost -> dim_product.cost | every SET reads the OLD row: cost gets the old list_price, not the new `cost * 2`

@ 61 S5 an explicit column list out of table order
value customers.full_name -> top_customers.full_name identity
value customers.id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value customers.country_code -> top_customers.region identity
forbid value customers.full_name -> top_customers.region | an explicit column list binds by ITS order, not the table's

@ 70 S6 an omitted column list, fewer values than columns
value orders.order_ts -> channel_mix.period_month derived
value orders.channel -> channel_mix.channel identity
forbid value orders.channel -> channel_mix.region | the omitted list binds to the FIRST columns in table order

@ 78 S7 RETURNING an expression from a DELETE (D-16)
value fct_shipment.cost -> <result>.doubled_cost derived
value fct_shipment.shipment_id -> <result>.shipment_id identity
filter fct_shipment.status -> fct_shipment
filter fct_shipment.status -> <result>

@ 87 S8 MERGE whose USING alias is the target's name
value dim_store.name -> dim_warehouse.name identity
forbid value dim_warehouse.name -> dim_warehouse.name | `dim_warehouse` here is the USING alias for core.dim_store

@ 98 S9 a correlated subquery in an UPDATE's WHERE
filter fct_order_line.product_key, dim_product.product_key -> dim_product
filter fct_order_line.quantity -> dim_product post
forbid value fct_order_line.quantity -> dim_product.status | the subquery is in WHERE: it decides which rows are updated; D-18 is about SET

@ 108 S10a a writable CTE read by a bare SELECT
filter web_events.event_ts -> web_events
filter web_events.event_ts -> <result>
note `removed` is COUNT(*): no value source. D-17: the predicate decides what is deleted and what is counted.

@ 122 S10b a writable CTE nothing reads
filter inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> inventory_snapshots
note PostgreSQL executes it regardless; losing this is losing a write silently.

@ 134 S11 ON CONFLICT ON CONSTRAINT, DO UPDATE WHERE on EXCLUDED
value inventory_snapshots.snapshot_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value inventory_snapshots.warehouse_id -> sales_daily.store_id identity
value inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> sales_daily.units identity
filter inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> sales_daily
forbid filter inventory_snapshots.snapshot_date -> sales_daily | sales_daily_uk's columns are the conflict target: structural (D-15)
